e/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"`[[skills]]` `resolved.checksum`"},"1417":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-41","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"For each legacy value, the command checks the installed content against it, computes the current\nform from that same content, and writes it. Every other byte of each file is kept, including\ncomments and formatting."},"1418":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-42","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A skill or override is checked against its installed directory."},"1419":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-43","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A bundle is re-pinned only when every legacy member digest matches: an overridden member is\nchecked against the cached bundle artifact, every other member against its installed directory.\nThe release digest is recomputed from the new member digests."},"1420":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-44","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A bundle history release is checked against its cached artifact in `.fastskill/bundles/`, or,\nwhen that is missing, against the bundle's Lock entry."},"1421":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-45","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A legacy value whose content is not installed, or whose installed content no longer matches it, is\nleft as it is and reported with the reason. Run `fastskill project install` to restore the content,\nthen run `project repin` again."},"1422":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-46","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"Bundle artifacts are immutable, so the command does not rewrite them. It reports each artifact\nthat still declares legacy member digests (in `.fastskill/bundles/`, in the Lock, or in the\nmanifest's `[bundles]`). Rebuild each one with `fastskill bundle build`."},"1423":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-47","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#find-legacy-digests-in-ci","content":"`--check` reports what a re-pin would do and changes nothing. It exits non-zero while any legacy\nvalue remains, so a CI job fails until the records are re-pinned and committed."},"1424":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-48","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#machine-readable-output","content":"The result uses the lifecycle envelope shared by the other project commands: `scope`, `outcome`\n(`changed`, `unchanged`, or `blocked`), `dry_run`, and one `targets` entry per legacy value with its\n`record`, `file`, `current_revision` (the legacy value), `target_revision` (the current form, when it\ncan be re-pinned), `changes`, and `retained` reasons. `legacy_artifacts` and `diagnostics` list the\nbundle artifacts to rebuild."},"1425":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-49","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"Code"},"1426":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-50","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"Meaning"},"1427":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-51","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"`0`"},"1428":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-52","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"No legacy digest remains (after a re-pin, or none was found)"},"1429":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-53","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"`1`"},"1430":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-54","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"A legacy value remains: under `--check`, or an entry left as is, or a legacy bundle artifact"},"1431":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-55","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"`2`"},"1432":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-56","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"No `skill-project.toml` was found, or a file could not be read or written"},"1433":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-57","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"A project without `skills.lock` has nothing to re-pin and exits `0`."},"1434":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-58","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#see-also","content":"project install - Restore the content a legacy value names"},"1435":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-59","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#see-also","content":"bundle commands - Rebuild a bundle artifact with `bundle build`"},"1436":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","type":"page","content":"repo commands","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Sources and distribution"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/repository-command"},"1437":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-0","page_id":"/cli-referenc