hat holds it:"},"1632":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-195","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#bearer-token","content":"FastSkill sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. If the variable is unset or empty,\nevery request to that registry fails; FastSkill never falls back to an\nunauthenticated request."},"1633":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-196","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"When the token is short-lived, a program can print it: an identity provider CLI, or a\nscript that performs a CI job's token exchange. A credential command can only be\nsaved to your user `repositories.toml`, so `--auth-type command` requires `--user`.\nA `skill-project.toml` that names a command is refused."},"1634":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-197","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"The program runs directly, without a shell, from FastSkill's configuration\ndirectory, and is stopped after 30 seconds."},"1635":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-198","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"The first line of its standard output is the token. More than 16 KiB of output, an\nempty token, or a non-zero exit fails the request. Errors name the program and its\nexit status, never the token."},"1636":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-199","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"Standard error reaches your terminal only when there is one. When standard input\nor standard error is not a terminal, FastSkill sets `FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0`, and\nthe command must print a token without prompting or exit non-zero."},"1637":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-200","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"It runs at most once per FastSkill process for each repository, and the token is\nkept in memory only."},"1638":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-201","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"With `bearer` and `command`, the token is sent only to the origin of the registry's\nindex URL. Downloads on other origins get no token, a redirect to another origin\ndrops it, and a redirect from `https` to `http` is refused. `repo list` and `repo info`\nshow the auth type, never the token."},"1639":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-202","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"Git sources use system Git credentials. A project manifest may use `pat` or `bearer`\nfor HTTP catalogs. See sources."},"1640":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-203","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"FastSkill supports multiple sources with priority-based resolution:"},"1641":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-204","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"**Resolution process**:"},"1642":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-205","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"Repositories are consulted in ascending priority order (0 before 1 before 2)."},"1643":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-206","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"The first repository that satisfies the lookup wins for that skill id."},"1644":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-207","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"Lower numeric priority means earlier in that order (0 is tried before 10)."},"1645":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-208","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"**Example**:"},"1646":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-209","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"`public-registry` (priority 0): `pptx v1.0.0`"},"1647":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-210","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"`team-skills` (priority 1): `pptx v1.2.0`"},"1648":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-211","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"Result: `pptx v1.0.0` from `public-registry` is used because priority 0 is consulted first."},"1649":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-212","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#creating-a-git-marketplace","content":"`--owner-name` is required: Claude Code rejects a marketplace without an\nowner. Run `claude plugin validate .` to check the generated file against\nClaude Code's own rules."},"1650":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-213","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"**Check name**: Ensure the repository name matches what you added."},"1651":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-214","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"**Verify credentials**:"},"1652":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-215","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"**Verify priority values**: Lower numbers have higher priority."},"1653":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-216","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"Priority 0 is highest, priority 10 is lower."},"1654":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-217","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"Repositories configuration is stored in `skill-project.toml` and should be committed to version control. Authentication credentials (environment variables) should never be committed. Per-machine repositories, including any credential command, live in `repositories.toml` in FastSkill's configuration directory (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fastskill/` when set) and take precedence over a project repository with the same name."},"1655":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-218","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#see-also","content":"Search Command - Semantic search for installed skills"},"1656":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-219","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#see-also","content":"Install Command - Installing skills from repositories"},"1657":{"id":"/cli-reference