the server is **read-only** unless this flag is passed."},"1749":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-27","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#options","content":"`false`"},"1750":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-28","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#read-only-by-default","content":"`fastskill server serve` is **read-only by default**. Read endpoints (list/get skills,\nproject, search, resolve, status, registry browse, the dashboard) are always available; every\nstate-changing endpoint (see the *write* rows in Core Endpoints) is &#x2A;*disabled\nunless you start the server with `--enable-write`**."},"1751":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-29","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#read-only-by-default","content":"When writes are disabled, a request to a write endpoint returns:"},"1752":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-30","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#read-only-by-default","content":"Run `fastskill server serve --enable-write` when you want to manage skills (install / update / remove) from\nthe web UI or API on your own machine."},"1753":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-31","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#security-model","content":"`fastskill server serve` is **not a security boundary**: it enforces no authentication of its own (no token\nendpoint; API routes require no `Authorization`/`x-api-key` header). It is designed to run\n**local-first** on your machine."},"1754":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-32","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#security-model","content":"If you expose the server on a shared or untrusted network, put an **authenticating reverse proxy or\nsidecar** in front of it and ensure the app port is not directly reachable — the proxy owns request\nauthentication. Combined with the read-only default, this means an exposed instance without\n`--enable-write` cannot be used to mutate state even before the proxy is considered."},"1755":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-33","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#api-base-path","content":"All application routes use the `/api/v1/…` namespace."},"1756":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-34","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#health-probes","content":"The server exposes two standard health endpoints immediately after startup:"},"1757":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-35","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#health-probes","content":"`GET /healthz` — Liveness probe. Returns HTTP 200 with a JSON body containing the fastskill\ncrate version, e.g. `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"version\":\"<current-release>\"}`."},"1758":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-36","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#health-probes","content":"`GET /readyz` — Readiness probe. Returns HTTP 200 when the server is ready to accept traffic.\nReturns HTTP 503 while graceful shutdown is in progress."},"1759":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-37","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#health-probes","content":"These endpoints are suitable for use with container orchestrators (Kubernetes, ECS, Docker)."},"1760":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-38","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#response-headers","content":"Every `/api/v1/…` response includes:"},"1761":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-39","page_id":"/cli-reference