ommand supports that\nscope. `--skills-dir <PATH>` overrides the installation directory for one invocation. In project\nmode fastskill warns that subsequent project commands must use the same override to inspect the\nsame installed state. `-v, --verbose` enables diagnostic logs."},"1858":{"id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/skill-commands#skill-add","content":"`SOURCE` can be a local directory, local ZIP, Git URL, remote ZIP URL, or skill ID. An existing\nrelative path wins over the skill-ID shorthand. Use `./name` when a nonexistent local path would\notherwise look like an ID."},"1859":{"id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/skill-commands#skill-add","content":"A skill ID is bare (`reviewer`) or, for an `http-registry` skill, scoped by its publisher\n(`acme/reviewer`). `--repository` looks it up in that repository only. Without it, the ID resolves\nagainst the highest-priority repository that lists it. A higher-priority repository is passed over\nonly when its refreshed (or, with `--offline`, cached) metadata shows the skill is absent."},"1860":{"id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/skill-commands#skill-add","content":"Option"},"1861":{"id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/skill-commands#skill-add","content":"Description"},"1862":{"id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/skill-commands#skill-add","content":"`--source-type <registry\\|github\\|git\\|local>`"},"1863":{"id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/skill-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/skill-commands#skill-add","content