":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#ci-usage-pattern","content":"CI usage pattern"},"2179":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-6","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Practical gating policy"},"2180":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-7","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"See also"},"2181":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-8","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-evals","content":"This workflow is the day-to-day path for quality checks. If you haven't authored a suite yet — the `[tool.fastskill.eval]` table, prompts CSV, and checks TOML — start with Eval setup first; pass/fail behavior (especially the inert `should_trigger` column, choosing between `skill_invoked` and `trigger_expectation`, and what `required = false` does) is documented there."},"2182":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-9","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-evals","content":"`--output-dir` is required on every `eval run` invocation — there is no default output location. All examples below include it. Each run lands under `<output-dir>/<timestamp>/<agent>/` (a numeric suffix is appended if that timestamp directory already exists) — that per-agent directory, not `<output-dir>` itself, is what `--run-dir` expects below."},"2183":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-10","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-the-suite","content":"**Runs are isolated by default.** Each case executes in a per-case scratch workspace containing only the skill under test (`SKILL.md` beside `skill-project.toml`, named by `[metadata].id`), with user-level skill discovery suppressed where the backend supports it. The `isolation:` line in the output (and the `isolation` object in `summary.json`) reports what each run actually got; a failed case's workspace survives under `<run-dir>/workspaces/` for debugging. Pass `--no-isolation` to run in the project root against your machine's ambient environment — and expect trigger rates measured before isolation existed to re-baseline on the first isolated run."},"2184":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-11","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-the-suite","content":"Common focused runs:"},"2185":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-12","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#summarize-the-run","content":"Use this for release notes and quick stakeholder review."},"2186":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-13","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#re-score-without-re-running-agent","content":"Use this when scoring logic changed and you want consistency across previous runs."},"2187":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-14","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Block merge if smoke tag fails"},"2188":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-15","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Block release if full suite fails"},"2189":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-16","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Keep per-tag pass-rate trends to detect slow quality drift"},"2190":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-17","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"Eval setup"},"2191":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-18","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2192":{"id":"/e