mmand_count","content":"Passes if the number of **tool invocations** the agent made is `<= limit`."},"2366":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-172","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"A tool invocation is a structured `tool_use` trace event, plus any `raw_json` trace line — the\nlatter covers backends that still emit tool calls as raw JSON instead of decoded tool events.\nAssistant text output, token-usage events, and unmodelled SDK event variants are **not** counted."},"2367":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-173","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Results use `\"check_name\": \"max_tool_calls\"`. The per-case artifact field counting\nthese events is `command_count`."},"2368":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-174","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Every check type accepts `required` (default `true`). Setting `required = false` makes the check **advisory**: it still runs, and its result still appears in the run artifacts with its own `passed` value, but a failure does not fail the case."},"2369":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-175","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Use it for signal you want visible in reports without gating the suite on it."},"2370":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-176","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"No `checks` file configured (or it loads zero explicit checks): the case still receives the required trigger expectation generated from `should_trigger`."},"2371":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-177","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Any checks loaded: the case **passes** only if every **required** check's `passed` is `true`. Checks marked `required = false` are reported but never fail the case. Among required checks there is no partial credit and no threshold — they are all-or-nothing per case."},"2372":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-178","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."},"2373":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-179","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A trial that times out is always `error`, independent of checks."},"2374":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-180","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Across trials, `pass_threshold` decides the case's aggregated status: pass rate across trials must be `>= pass_threshold`."},"2375":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-181","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"Once the manifest, CSV, and checks file exist:"},"2376":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-182","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--output-dir` is **required** on `fastskill eval run` — there is no default. Omitting it fails argument parsing before anything else runs:"},"2377":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-183","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive on both `eval run` and `eval validate` — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` additionally requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`); on `eval validate` both are optional — omit them to validate config without checking any agent's availability."},"2378":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-184","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"See Run evals for the full day-to-day command set, artifact layout, and CI gating pattern."},"2379":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-185","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`[tool.fastskill.eval]` present with a `prompts` path that resolves."},"2380":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-186","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Prompts CSV has `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger` headers (plus `tags` / `workspace_subdir` if you use them)."},"2381":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-187","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Each `should_trigger` value reflects the required consultation/non-consultation expectation; explicit `skill_invoked` checks do not contradict it."},"2382":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-188","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Outcome correctness is measured separately where consultation alone is insufficient."},"2383":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-189","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`fastskill eval validate --all` passes and lists the agent you intend to run against as available."},"2384":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-190","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Out