sted CLI write path."],[3006,"The registry index uses a simple org/package directory structure:"],[3196,"The registry validates `marketplace.json` files:"],[985,"The report"],[2956,"The response ranks installed skills by relevance to the prompt so the agent can pull just the top\nmatches into context. `resolve` is a **read** endpoint — it works whether or not `server serve` was started\nwith `--enable-write`."],[512,"The result is `dist/notes-team-1.0.0.zip`. Its embedded identity, version, membership, and\ndigests are authoritative, so renaming the download does not change the release.\nAn artifact built by an earlier release, whose digests lack the `sha256-tree-v2:` prefix, still\ninstalls with a warning; rebuild it to record current-form digests."],[1424,"The result uses the lifecycle envelope shared by the other project commands: `scope`, `outcome`\n(`changed`, `unchanged`, or `blocked`), `dry_run`, and one `targets` entry per legacy value with its\n`record`, `file`, `current_revision` (the legacy value), `target_revision` (the current form, when it\ncan be re-pinned), `changes`, and `retained` reasons. `legacy_artifacts` and `diagnostics` list the\nbundle artifacts to rebuild."],[2846,"The run directory is safe to copy, archive, or share. Resume and inspect commands only need this directory."],[2698,"The run directory records every step's artifacts for inspection."],[723,"The runs under `--root` carry more than one `(agent, model)`"],[351,"The safest way to recover is to delete the corrupted lock and regenerate it:"],[726,"The same case id is measured by more than one run"],[2932,"The same trap applies if every check you configure is `required = false`: scoring filters to required checks, so an all-advisory file leaves nothing to score and every case reads `1.0`. Keep at least one required check."],[249,"The script picks the archive for your platform, checks it against the release's\n`SHA256SUMS`, installs `fastskill` into `~/.local/bin` (`%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin` on\nWindows) and adds that directory to PATH. Open a new shell, then run `fastskill -V`."],[2442,"The server exposes read-only tools by default. Mutating tools require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`. Tool names use the full command path, for example\n`fastskill_skill_read` and `fastskill_project_install`. See\nMCP tool access for write configuration."],[1756,"The server exposes two standard health endpoints immediately after startup:"],[3299,"The server has no built-in authentication. Use it locally, or put authentication\nand network restrictions in front of it when exposing it to other users. Read-only\naccess still reveals skill content. See the security model."],[3517,"The server is **read-only by default**: the mutating commands are not exported as tools unless you\nstart it with `--enable-write`. See Write access below."],[524,"The shared Manifest can declare skills from multiple Git repositories, configured repositories,\nZIP URLs, or shared paths. `project install` resolves the combined roots and the consuming project\nwrites the exact results to its own `skills.lock`. References may be nested. FastSkill rejects\nmissing files, reference cycles, and incompatible declarations of the same skill ID."],[835,"The skill ID (directory name) must meet these requirements:"],[3400,"The skills directory contains the installed files an agent reads."],[3464,"The skills directory exists and is a directory"],[995,"The source and the signing keys come only from two files, never from a project:"],[999,"The source is either a local file or an `https://` URL."],[3447,"The standard validator expects a lowercase name of 1–64 characters using letters,\ndigits, and single separating hyphens. The description must be nonempty and at most\n1024 characters. Name and description help an agent decide when to load the skill."],[2672,"The suite CSV has zero cases tagged `selection`. Exact message: `OPTIMIZE_NO_SELECTION_CASES: suite has zero cases tagged 'selection'`."],[2674,"The suite CSV has zero cases tagged `train` (e.g. every row is `selection`/`test`). See Setup for the exact message and the full split model."],[2863,"The suite is a CSV file with one row per eval case. Required columns:"],[2263,"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."],[631,"The summary reports what each run actually got (`isolation:` line in table output, `isolation` object in `summary.json`), and a failed case's scratch workspace is kept under `<run-dir>/workspaces/` for debugging. Pass `--no-isolation` to restore the old inherit-everything behaviour."],[996,"the system file, deployed by device management: `/etc/fastskill/managed.toml` (Linux),\n`/Library/Application Support/FastSkill/managed.toml` (macOS) or\n`%ProgramData%\\FastSkill\\managed.toml` (Windows). It must be owned by the administrator and\nwritable by nobody else;"],[2952,"The task text to resolve against. Must not be empty (`RESOLVE_EMPTY_PROMPT`)."],[2853,"The three splits"],[3286,"The token is sent only to the origin (scheme, host and port) of `index_url`. A\ndownload on another origin gets no token and must carry its own authorization, such\nas a pre-signed URL. A redirect to another origin is followed without the token, and\na redirect from `https` to `http` is refused."],[3283,"The token is the first line of standard output with the trailing line ending\nremoved. Output over 16 KiB, an empty token, or a non-zero exit is an error. Errors\nname the program and its exit status, never the token."],[1183,"The tree contains 50 leaf commands. Root help shows the namespaces as a compact table of contents.\nRun `fastskill <namespace> --help` to discover that namespace, then run\n`fastskill <namespace> <action> --help` for arguments and examples. A bare skill ID is not a\ncommand; use `fastskill skill read <skill-id>`."],[3432,"The two `managed-` values appear only when this machine follows a verified managed state (see\n`fastskill managed`). They take precedence over every other\nvalue, `managed-blocked` first, and `skill list --check` fails on them even for a skill outside\nthe current selection."],[3458,"The two tools for debugging FastSkill are `fastskill cli doctor` — an environment/configuration health\ncheck — and the global `--verbose` / `-v` flag for detailed command output."],[997,"the user file, `managed.toml` in FastSkill's configuration folder."],[2872,"The user message sent to the target agent."],[2818,"The usual cause is a suite with no `train` rows, which `optimization run` now rejects up front\nwith `OPTIMIZE_NO_TRAIN_CASES` (see Setup). This warning is the\nbackstop for every other way a run can end up doing nothing — for example a loop\nconfiguration that yields no steps. Treat it as a failed run, not a successful one:\n`best_skill.md` is the seed document, unchanged."],[3487,"The way you test a skill in FastSkill is `fastskill eval`. You define eval cases in your project\nmanifest, run them against an agent, and score the results. There is no separate unit/mock harness —\neval is the testing framework."],[517,"Then restore the exact locked release:"],[2963,"There are no cache-size, eviction, or tuning knobs to configure. Resolution is driven by the prompt,\nthe `limit`, and the embedding index — not by a configurable runtime cache."],[2760,"There is **no `skips.json` artifact**. Skip information is derived from `update.json`,\nwhich records how the step's edit budget was spent:"],[2923,"There is **no** `type`, `id`, or `weight` field, and there is no LLM-judge/rubric check type — scoring is purely deterministic pattern/file/count matching against the captured transcript."],[513,"There is no `[bundle.members]` list to maintain. A source Manifest using the earlier `[bundle]`\nformat remains buildable for migration, while all new bundles should use `[metadata]`."],[2428,"These are all read endpoints and work without `--enable-write